00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:10.314
So I... I've always had
a deep affinity for this city.


00:03:12.359 --> 00:03:14.304
A lot of people are saying,
"You can't do it."


00:03:14.328 --> 00:03:18.309
This is the fifth most
violent city in the country,


00:03:18.333 --> 00:03:22.045
and people are going,
"Detroit? Really, Detroit?


00:03:22.069 --> 00:03:23.814
Sweetheart, there's other places


00:03:23.839 --> 00:03:25.850
you'd get a lot further
with than Detroit."


00:03:25.874 --> 00:03:29.587
But I say, "Sweetheart you,
that's where we're starting"


00:03:29.611 --> 00:03:32.590
A lot of people just don't
know about this problem,


00:03:32.614 --> 00:03:34.992
and I was one of those people.


00:03:35.016 --> 00:03:37.062
And then you meet
people like Kym Worthy


00:03:37.086 --> 00:03:39.229
and you see what she's doing,


00:03:39.254 --> 00:03:42.268
you sort of can't help but
say, "What am I doing?


00:03:43.993 --> 00:03:46.071
When I first met Kym
four years ago,


00:03:46.095 --> 00:03:50.375
Detroit had just discovered
11,000 untested kits.


00:03:50.399 --> 00:03:53.946
Kym's commitment to test
every last kit


00:03:53.971 --> 00:03:57.049
here in Detroit,
is so remarkable.


00:03:57.073 --> 00:04:00.353
I've been playing Detective
Benson on "SVU" for 15 years,


00:04:00.377 --> 00:04:03.922
and when I first began, letters
started coming in from viewers.


00:04:03.946 --> 00:04:07.626
These men and women
were disclosing to me


00:04:07.651 --> 00:04:09.085
their stories of abuse.


00:04:11.088 --> 00:04:13.633
And at first, it was a few,
then it was more,


00:04:13.657 --> 00:04:16.236
then it was hundreds,
and then it was thousands.


00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:21.608
A majority of them included
some version of,


00:04:21.632 --> 00:04:24.311
"I've never told
this to anybody before."


00:04:24.335 --> 00:04:29.648
And here I was, an actress on
a TV show getting these letters,


00:04:29.673 --> 00:04:32.052
and I was immersed
in these issues.


00:04:32.076 --> 00:04:35.944
So I educated myself,
and I got involved.


00:04:37.081 --> 00:04:38.924
To me, the rape kit backlog


00:04:38.949 --> 00:04:42.630
is the clearest
and most shocking demonstration


00:04:42.654 --> 00:04:44.598
of how we regard these crimes.


00:04:44.622 --> 00:04:48.068
Kym's tireless and relentless
work here in Detroit


00:04:48.092 --> 00:04:50.925
is unwavering and unstoppable.


00:04:51.996 --> 00:04:54.307
I had absolutely no clue


00:04:54.332 --> 00:04:56.744
that people stockpiled
rape kits.


00:04:56.768 --> 00:05:00.215
I had no clue
that anyone would do that.


00:05:04.609 --> 00:05:08.069
I just never imagined
that it was anyplace else than here.


00:05:12.217 --> 00:05:14.562
I was asked
by the Detroit Police Department


00:05:14.587 --> 00:05:19.001
to accompany them
to an off site property room.


00:05:19.025 --> 00:05:20.668
I went there.
During that time,


00:05:20.693 --> 00:05:22.337
I noticed the racks with boxes


00:05:22.361 --> 00:05:24.139
with rape kits in them.


00:05:24.163 --> 00:05:26.676
And I asked,
"What's in those boxes?"


00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.177
And they said that those
were old tested rape kits.


00:05:29.201 --> 00:05:31.313
But I pulled some of the boxes,


00:05:31.338 --> 00:05:34.016
and I realized that there
still was the seal on the kits.


00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.319
<i>Which would lead you to
believe they had never been tested</i>


00:05:36.343 --> 00:05:38.621
if the seal's never been broken.


00:05:38.645 --> 00:05:42.960
I was extremely shocked to think
that there was just racks of kits


00:05:42.984 --> 00:05:44.695
sitting
in an abandoned warehouse


00:05:44.719 --> 00:05:48.732
with windows open
and birds flying around.


00:05:48.756 --> 00:05:52.068
He said, "Boss, you're not going to
believe what has happened, or what I saw."


00:05:52.093 --> 00:05:54.705
And he said, "I think I saw,"


00:05:54.729 --> 00:05:58.375
